<title>NORWAY: Saga said to mull bid for Kuwaiti KPC's Santa Fe.</title>
<headline>Saga said to mull bid for Kuwaiti KPC's Santa Fe.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's largest independent oil company Saga Petroleum ASA is considering bidding for British-based Sante Fe Exploration, the business daily Dagens Naeringsliv (DN) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Santa Fe is valued at around $1 billion and Saga is expected to make an offer by November 1, DN said.</p>
<p>&quot;Saga is evaluating the company at the moment, but they haven't made a formal offer yet,&quot; Michael Bourgeois, managing director in Sante Fe, was quoted as telling DN.</p>
<p>Saga spokesman Andreas Qvale could not confirm that the company was due to make a bid for Sante Fe.</p>
</text>
